.venv/
_bench_tmp/
__pycache__/

# Derived artifacts. `build_corpus.py` emits pages/; `capture.py` emits shots/ and
# snapshots/. The generators plus manifest.json are the source of truth, and
# regenerating is two commands -- committing ~47k lines of rendered output would
# bury the evidence that actually matters (findings_dom.json, local_vlm_results.json,
# blind_key.json) in noise that changes on every Chromium bump.
corpus/out/pages/
corpus/out/shots/
corpus/out/snapshots/
corpus/out/blind/

# Same rule, applied to the router's output. `route_plan.json` is 92 KB of which
# almost all is the six unconditional questions repeated once per page, and
# crops/ is the rendered image ledger -- both regenerate from the committed
# findings in one command (`bash run.sh`). The evidence worth keeping is the
# findings files and the README table they support; a plan file that changes
# whenever a caption is reworded would bury exactly that.
corpus/out/route_plan.json
corpus/out/crops/
# The second capture scale exists to prove the pixel arms agree across it, which
# is a property the run asserts rather than an artifact anyone reads.
corpus/out/findings_xcheck@*.json
